{"batchcomplete":true,"query":{"pages":[{"pageid":206242,"ns":0,"title":"Differential (mechanical device)","extract":"A differential is a gear train with three drive shafts that has the property that the rotational speed of one shaft is the average of the speeds of the others. A common use of differentials is in motor vehicles, to allow the wheels at each end of a drive axle to rotate at different speeds while cornering.","description":"Type of simple planetary gear train","descriptionsource":"local"}]}}